//? Title: Tree sort: actual insertion paths and in-order emission
//? Subtitle: Actual native state, retained fixtures and explicit limits
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Sorting integers through an unbalanced search tree is simple, but ordered inputs
can make insertion quadratic. We inspect the actual tree and its traversal, then
measure the executed comparisons.
)

\toc

> The method

Each insertion follows left when the new key is smaller and right otherwise. By
induction every left subtree precedes its root, which precedes its right
subtree. In-order traversal therefore emits a nondecreasing sequence. Insertion
comparisons equal the sum of inserted-node depths. Sorted distinct input gives
n(n−1)/2 comparisons; the iterative traversal uses O(n) storage and avoids
recursive stack exhaustion.

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/tree_sort_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/tree_sort.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::tree_sort_work({3, 1, 2});
    std::print("| node | key | left | right | depth |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < r.values.size(); ++i)
        std::print("|{}|{}|{}|{}|{}|\n", i, r.values[i], r.left[i], r.right[i],
                   r.depth[i]);
    std::print("\nSorted `{}`; comparisons {}.\n", r.sorted, r.comparisons);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Insert 3,1,2");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual comparisons", r.comparisons));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual in-order {}", r.sorted));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/tree_sort_tiny.svg");
}
```
